<title>INDIA: India clears foreign projects of 26.7 bln rupees.</title>
<headline>India clears foreign projects of 26.7 bln rupees.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian government on Friday approved projects involving foreign direct investment (FDI) worth 26.74 billion rupees, a statement said.  </p>
<p>The statement said the industry ministry cleared 84 proposals.</p>
<p>The projects are expected to earn 67.23 billion rupees from exports over a period of five years, the statement said.</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom +91-11-301 2024</p>
</text>
